title: 'fungible(s): Check deposit against capped amount in best-effort `release`'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    With `Precision::BestEffort`, `release()` called `can_deposit` with
    the
       requested amount but released only what was actually held. If free
    plus
       held was below the existential deposit, `increase_balance` credited
       nothing while the hold had already been reduced. The funds were lost
       without any change to total issuance.

       Cap the amount at the held balance first, call `can_deposit` with
    that
       capped amount, and then decrease the hold with `Exact`. A release
    that
       can't be credited now fails with `CannotCreate` and changes nothing.

       Applies to both `fungible::hold::Mutate` and
    `fungibles::hold::Mutate`.
       Adds a regression test in `pallet-balances`.
crates:
- name: pallet-balances
  bump: patch
- name: frame-support
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-assets-holder
  bump: patch
